1. First, calculate the number of indoor plants: The number of indoor plants is one-fourth of the total number of plants, so (1/4) * 100 = 25 plants. 2. Next, calculate the number of plants remaining after removing the indoor plants: The number of remaining plants is 100 - 25 = 75 plants. 3. Next, calculate the number of outdoor plants: The number of outdoor plants is two-thirds of the remaining plants, so (2/3) * 75 = 50 plants. 4. Next, calculate the number of flowering plants: The number of flowering plants is the total number of plants minus the indoor plants and the outdoor plants, so 100 - 25 - 50 = 25 plants. 5. Calculate the percentage of flowering plants: The percentage of flowering plants is the number of flowering plants divided by the total number of plants, multiplied by 100: (25 / 100) * 100 = 25%.

Therefore, 25% of the plants are flowering plants.

\boxed{25}
